Here's the base I use most — it spins glossy every time.

```recipe-card
{
  "title": "Ninja Creami Vanilla Bean Ice Cream",
  "description": "A creamy, no-churn base built for the Creami's spin cycle \u2014 freeze it flat, spin it twice, and it comes out like gelato.",
  "base_servings": 4,
  "prep_time": "10 min",
  "total_time": "24 hr (mostly freezing)",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "equipment": "Ninja Creami",
  "ingredients": [
    {
      "id": "cream",
      "name": "heavy cream",
      "amount": 1,
      "unit": "cup"
    },
    {
      "id": "milk",
      "name": "whole milk",
      "amount": "1 1/2",
      "unit": "cups"
    },
    {
      "id": "sugar",
      "name": "granulated sugar",
      "amount": 0.5,
      "unit": "cup"
    },
    {
      "id": "vanilla",
      "name": "vanilla bean paste",
      "amount": 2,
      "unit": "tsp"
    },
    {
      "id": "cheese",
      "name": "cream cheese",
      "amount": 2,
      "unit": "tbsp",
      "note": "softened"
    },
    {
      "id": "salt",
      "name": "fine sea salt",
      "amount": "a pinch"
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Whisk the base",
      "content": "Beat the softened cream cheese smooth, then whisk in the sugar, milk, cream, vanilla and salt until no grains remain.",
      "timer_seconds": 120
    },
    {
      "title": "Freeze flat",
      "content": "Pour into the Creami pint, level it, lid on, and freeze on a flat shelf for a full 24 hours.",
      "timer_seconds": 86400
    },
    {
      "title": "First spin",
      "content": "Run the ICE CREAM program. It will look crumbly and powdery \u2014 that is expected.",
      "timer_seconds": 180
    },
    {
      "title": "Re-spin",
      "content": "Add 1 tbsp milk and run RE-SPIN until it turns glossy and scoopable.",
      "timer_seconds": 120
    },
    {
      "title": "Serve",
      "content": "Scoop immediately, or firm up in the freezer for 20 minutes for a denser scoop."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Cream cheese is the stabiliser \u2014 skip it and you get icy shards.",
    "If the pint is domed after freezing, let it sit 3 minutes before spinning or the blade will stall."
  ]
}
```

Freeze it flat and give it a full 24 hours before the first spin.

